<title>UK: Nomura sets calls on leading football clubs index.</title>
<headline>Nomura sets calls on leading football clubs index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nomura International Plc said it</p>
<p>has issued four million European-style call warrants, on a index</p>
<p>of leading English football clubs.</p>
<p>The football clubs included are Manchester United,</p>
<p>Arsenal, Chelsea village, Liverpool, Everton, Tottenham</p>
<p>Hotspur, Caspian (Leeds United), Aston Villa</p>
<p>and West Ham.</p>
<p>One index is controlled by 100 warrants.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE    90.0 STG		  ISSUE PRICE 3.45 STG</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	31.DEC.98		 LISTING     LUXEMBOURG</p>
<p>SPOT REFERENCE  100 STG</p>
<p> NOTES    OTHER PREMIER LEAGUE CLUBS WILL BE ADDED TO THE</p>
<p>	    INDEX AS THEIR SHARES BECOME PUBLICLY AVAILABLE.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
